The pass-31 prompts are lost, so I will build a new generation set and run it with "both". Original and bp1 replies then come from identical prompts, and the pass also counts how many replies differ. The set covers:
- no-guess questions;
- correct guesses in the training phrasing (CG), which became stray digits under supp3 and bp3;
- wrong guesses in the training phrasing and in several new phrasings;
- context-copy prompts;
- a few open-ended requests.

If bp1 answers no-guess and context-copy prompts like the original, and answers wrong-guess prompts with the correct answer or at least not with digits, the degeneration came from the L11H3 amplification and bp1 is the cleaner edit. If bp1 also produces digits, both candidates share the defect.

